    "holder": "National Gallery of Art, Washington",
    "credit": "Public domain · image via Wikimedia Commons",
    "story": "Monet's wife Camille stands on a hill near their home at Argenteuil, with their son Jean a little way behind her in the meadow. We look up at her against the sky, as if from the grass. It is a windy summer day: her veil and white dress blow sideways, the clouds race, the flowers bend. Monet painted it in the open air, with quick loose strokes that catch the breeze rather than every detail."
